{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I can see your account was locked after several failed sign-in attempts from your usual office network. I've asked a technician to unlock it, and that approval is queued now. It hasn't been unlocked yet, so please wait for the confirmation before trying again. Once it's unlocked, if you're locked out again soon, check whether an old password is saved on your phone's mail app or another device and update it, because that's the usual cause. If you still can't get in after the unlock, reply here and we'll move quickly on your month-end close.",
  "internal_note": "User tom.becker (user_id 4), Finance, BL-LT-0104. Account status: locked, 5 failed_login_count, sign_in_blocked false, password last set 2026-07-23, must_change_password false. Sign-in logs (14 days): 5 failed_password attempts on 2026-10-09 between 09:20 and 09:32 New York time, all from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 during usual hours. Each failure was interleaved with the user's own successful Duo push sign-ins from the same IP, and there were no hosting, foreign, or overnight sign-ins. This fits KB-001 (saved old password or mistyping), not KB-031. Unlock queued as approval_id 1. Not run yet. Follow-up: confirm the user has updated saved passwords on phone mail and other devices. If the account locks again within an hour of unlocking, escalate per KB-001. No password reset was requested. Priority P2 with month-end close today.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
